      "start_seconds": 6.11,
      "end_seconds": 13.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Uh, morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.81,
      "end_seconds": 18.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.71,
      "end_seconds": 29.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "uh, uh, I've been feeling very unwell, and I wanted to get it checked"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.55,
      "end_seconds": 34.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.4,
      "end_seconds": 45.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "Six months, I think... sorry, about three months, I got that wrong i've never really been one for hospitals"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.05,
      "end_seconds": 50.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.82,
      "end_seconds": 54.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I, I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.21,
      "end_seconds": 57.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.11,
      "end_seconds": 97.92,
      "duration_seconds": 38.81,
      "text": "Actually, when it starts I tend to get severe pain in the upper tummy going through to the back as well. Oh, and a fast heart. Sorry, um, what was I saying, the severe pain in the upper tummy going through to the back? That's been since last Tuesday. About severe pain in the upper tummy going through to the back, I'd say mild. Vomiting was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.99,
      "end_seconds": 102.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.41,
      "end_seconds": 117.51,
      "duration_seconds": 14.1,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I look after my grandchildren most days. No, I share a house with my brother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.96,
      "end_seconds": 121.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.1,
      "end_seconds": 129.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Ah, you know, just a a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.54,
      "end_seconds": 134.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.21,
      "end_seconds": 139.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.02,
      "end_seconds": 146.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.17,
      "end_seconds": 150.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Metoprolol I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.87,
      "end_seconds": 160.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.24,
      "end_seconds": 166.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.14,
      "end_seconds": 170.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.65,
      "end_seconds": 180.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "erm, I have heart failure, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.28,
      "end_seconds": 184.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Yes. Has there been any yellow eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.15,
      "end_seconds": 188.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "No, none, no yellow eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.24,
      "end_seconds": 193.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "a few quick ones: fever, black stools or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.57,
      "end_seconds": 199.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Erm, uh, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.98,
      "end_seconds": 202.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.06,
      "end_seconds": 205.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.72,
      "end_seconds": 210.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.82,
      "end_seconds": 225.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.18,
      "end_seconds": 244.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "okay: heart rate 121, SpO2 99 percent on room air, temperature is 36.8 degrees, blood pressure 134 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.24,
      "end_seconds": 249.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.95,
      "end_seconds": 264.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "sure thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.43,
      "end_seconds": 268.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "So, I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.77,
      "end_seconds": 287.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Your upper tummy is very tender and you look dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.88,
      "end_seconds": 291.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.82,
      "end_seconds": 304.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Taking everything into account, this is probably acute pancreatitis. I can't rule out gallstone disease yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.87,
      "end_seconds": 308.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.17,
      "end_seconds": 318.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now acute pancreatitis is my leading thought, not anything worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.99,
      "end_seconds": 355.31,
      "duration_seconds": 25.32,
      "text": "Let's get an abdominal scan, for pancreatitis. We should do an amylase blood test for severe abdominal pain. You need admission for fluids and pain relief, nothing to eat for now. I'll also refer you to the surgical team. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Book a review straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.01,
      "end_seconds": 360.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Okay, so okay, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.42,
      "end_seconds": 364.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.78,
      "end_seconds": 371.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "I mean, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
